   "start": 0.24,
   "text": "So where does it all go? Amino acids, monosaccharides and short-chain fatty acids enter the blood capillaries and travel through the hepatic portal vein to the liver. Long-chain fatty acids, packed into chylomicrons, take the lymphatic route, lacteal, lymphatic vessels, thoracic duct, and into the blood at the left subclavian vein."
  }
 ],
 "text": "So where does it all go? Amino acids, monosaccharides and short-chain fatty acids enter the blood capillaries and travel through the hepatic portal vein to the liver. Long-chain fatty acids, packed into chylomicrons, take the lymphatic route, lacteal, lymphatic vessels, thoracic duct, and into the blood at the left subclavian vein."
